.TH KICHAT 1 "2026-10-07" "KiChat" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kichat \- chat and research with a language model running on your own machine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kichat
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kichat
is a desktop application and has no command line: everything happens in the
window, and every option is in the settings view inside it.
.PP
It talks to a model served by LM Studio, by Ollama, or by any OpenAI-compatible
endpoint. When a question needs current information \- prices, laws, news, live
data \- it searches the web through Brave or DuckDuckGo and reads the pages it
finds. Documents you attach (PDF, DOCX, PPTX, Excel, plain text and Markdown) are
extracted and indexed locally. Long conversations are compacted automatically
before they overflow the model's context window, which is a reading instruction
rather than a deletion: the original messages stay in the database.
.PP
There is no account, no cloud and no telemetry. The network is used only for the
searches and model calls you ask for.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B kichat
reads no environment variables. Its configuration is the settings view, stored in
the database named under FILES.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kichat/kichat.db
Everything that matters: chats, messages, compactions, attached documents and
their full-text index, and the caches of searches and scraped pages.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kichat/secrets
The search API key, when the desktop keyring could not be used. The key is kept
in the keyring whenever one is available.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/kichat
Window and webview state: the HTTP cache, the HSTS list, media keys. Deleting it
costs nothing but a slower first page.
.SH NOTES
Expired entries are pruned from both web caches on every start, so the database
grows with your conversations rather than with your browsing.
.PP
Deleting
.I kichat.db
resets the application to a fresh installation. Deleting the directory resets
everything.
